  "generated_text": "1. **Identify the probability of each outcome:**\n   - Probability of an island having treasure and no traps: $\\frac{1}{4}$\n   - Probability of an island having traps but no treasure: $\\frac{1}{12}$\n   - Probability of an island having neither traps nor treasure: $\\frac{2}{3}$\n\n2. **Calculate the probability of encountering exactly 3 islands with treasure and none with traps:**\n   - The probability of exactly 3 islands with treasure and 3 islands with neither traps nor treasure is given by:\n     \\[\n     \\binom{6}{3} \\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)^3 \\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^3\n     \\]\n   - Simplify the expression:\n     \\[\n     \\binom{6}{3} \\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)^3 \\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^3 = 20 \\cdot \\frac{1}{64} \\cdot \\frac{8}{27} = \\frac{10}{432}\n     \\]\n\nConclusion:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{5}{216}}\n\\]",
  "grade": {
    "error": null,
    "extracted_answer": "[5/216, '\\\\frac{5}{216}']",
    "gold_answer": "There are $\\binom{6}{3}=20$ ways to choose 3 islands. For each of these choices, there is a probability of $\\left( \\frac{1}{4} \\right)^3 \\left( \\frac{2}{3} \\right)^3$ that the chosen islands have treasure and the remaining ones have neither treasure nor traps. Therefore, the probability that the pirate encounters exactly 3 islands with treasure and none with traps is $20 \\left( \\frac{1}{4} \\right)^3 \\left( \\frac{2}{3} \\right)^3 = \\boxed{\\frac{5}{54}}$.",
    "is_correct": false
